WEBVTT

00:07.765 --> 00:09.267
<i>It all happened the same year.</i>

00:09.892 --> 00:14.647
<i>In one country, the sun burned so hot,
it felt like hell, fire, and brimstone.</i>

00:15.398 --> 00:20.819
<i>In another, intense rains pelted down
for what seemed like an eternity.</i>

00:20.820 --> 00:24.281
<i>It left the lands battered
and incapable of producing crops,</i>

00:24.282 --> 00:28.327
<i>animals hungry and in dire straits,
and people's hearts in despair.</i>

00:29.954 --> 00:30.955
<i>But most crucially,</i>

00:31.789 --> 00:33.374
<i>it tilted the balance of power.</i>

00:34.167 --> 00:36.376
<i>Swords came to clash</i>

00:36.377 --> 00:38.379
<i>as people were consumed by hatred.</i>

00:44.343 --> 00:46.344
<i>Rule by might.</i>

00:46.345 --> 00:48.264
<i>Senseless warfare.</i>

00:50.183 --> 00:51.350
<i>Was that truly what...</i>

00:52.435 --> 00:55.146
<i>"he" would've wanted for these lands?</i>

02:36.038 --> 02:39.959
SPRING BY THE LAKE

02:53.931 --> 02:57.768
Insomniac, aren't we going to see
my father? We should hurry.

03:00.897 --> 03:01.730
What's all this?

03:01.731 --> 03:03.773
Is something the matter?

03:03.774 --> 03:07.861
Anna-Marie. We just got back and found
everyone in this room passed out.

03:07.862 --> 03:11.990
What? Where's the castellan?
He must be informed at once.

03:11.991 --> 03:13.909
We'll get him. Let's go, Insomniac.

03:13.910 --> 03:14.952
Okay.

03:19.790 --> 03:23.586
<i>Wait, did I nod off just now?</i>

03:26.130 --> 03:29.507
<i>Insomniac never felt drowsy or sleepy.</i>

03:29.508 --> 03:31.928
<i>But on this day, things were different.</i>

03:41.437 --> 03:43.521
<i>Here we have the seven knight brothers,</i>

03:43.522 --> 03:46.943
<i>starting another day in their lives.</i>

03:50.112 --> 03:52.490
It's time to wake up, Chilly.

03:53.282 --> 03:56.452
Aren't you glad a kitty cat
kept your head warm for you?

04:05.211 --> 04:07.254
Good morning, Lord Bruno.

04:09.882 --> 04:11.591
Morning, everyone.

04:11.592 --> 04:14.052
Did you have a fruitful night
of reading, Insomniac?

04:14.053 --> 04:16.263
I did. I got through two books last night.

04:17.974 --> 04:19.849
All right. I'm all warmed up.

04:19.850 --> 04:21.686
Morning, Moja.

04:22.812 --> 04:24.313
It's already morning?

04:24.897 --> 04:27.315
Get ready, Chilly.

04:27.316 --> 04:28.526
I know.

04:35.324 --> 04:37.659
Of course it'd be windy
on the fifth floor.

04:37.660 --> 04:39.536
Hurry on along.

04:39.537 --> 04:41.956
We're on storeroom duty today, right?

04:44.625 --> 04:45.917
Such a pleasant breeze.

04:45.918 --> 04:49.129
Hurry up, Feverish,
or you'll get yelled at again.

04:49.130 --> 04:50.089
Oh, man.

04:52.800 --> 04:55.428
I heard yesterday's herring
were too salty.

04:56.137 --> 04:58.304
Hey, we're out of flour.

04:58.305 --> 05:01.100
Somebody go get some oregano!

05:05.229 --> 05:08.523
Can I have some bread?
I'm going to need it very soon.

05:08.524 --> 05:11.652
Sure, as long as you're eating
yesterday's leftovers.

05:12.570 --> 05:14.696
We have lots of guests today.

05:14.697 --> 05:17.115
We must keep the pantry
stocked at all times.

05:17.116 --> 05:18.617
Got it!

05:19.452 --> 05:20.953
<i>Guests?</i>

05:24.081 --> 05:26.750
<i>I wonder if the margrave is here.</i>

05:26.751 --> 05:30.170
Quit spacing out, Chilly. You're on fire.

05:30.171 --> 05:31.422
Huh?

05:35.551 --> 05:37.343
Thanks, Colette.

05:37.344 --> 05:39.846
No wonder my leg felt so good.

05:39.847 --> 05:42.057
Is that it? The shiny scarf?

05:42.058 --> 05:45.269
Is that what the nobleman's son gave you?

05:45.853 --> 05:49.230
Your oldest brother was in here
crying last night.

05:49.231 --> 05:53.276
He said he didn't raise you to become
some provincial noble's plaything.

05:53.277 --> 05:55.779
Wait, how did we get to that?

05:55.780 --> 05:56.906
Hey, Chilly.

05:57.907 --> 05:59.616
I'll tell you something about nobles.

05:59.617 --> 06:02.744
They'll happily turn on even the king
to protect their land.

06:02.745 --> 06:05.997
And they never finish their food.
They have no appreciation for it.

06:05.998 --> 06:07.916
Remember, you're a royal knight.

06:07.917 --> 06:10.376
Don't get overly familiar
with just anybody.

06:10.377 --> 06:11.295
Right.

06:12.296 --> 06:14.506
We're good here. Go tend to your training.

06:14.507 --> 06:16.008
Got it. I'll do that.

06:20.554 --> 06:23.181
<i>Yeah, but when it's this peaceful,</i>

06:23.182 --> 06:26.935
<i>all we can really do
is help around the king's land.</i>

06:26.936 --> 06:29.230
<i>And entertain guests, I guess.</i>

06:29.939 --> 06:33.692
<i>But hey, let's just hope
we never get called into action.</i>

06:39.490 --> 06:43.243
You were always bad at this,
but you're laughable today.

06:43.244 --> 06:45.620
Is there something bothering you?

06:45.621 --> 06:47.456
No, not really.

06:48.916 --> 06:53.546
If you need relationship advice,
talk to me, the love master, Fraternity.

06:54.255 --> 06:58.717
Problem is, you won't really be much help
because your idea of love is so diverse.

06:59.969 --> 07:02.137
Sorry about that. Let me go cool off.

07:02.138 --> 07:04.973
Wait, Chilly. I'm only trying to help.

07:04.974 --> 07:07.809
Castellan, I can't draw this bowstring.

07:07.810 --> 07:10.186
You're trying too hard.

07:10.187 --> 07:13.314
These are bows for children.
They shouldn't be that tight.

07:13.315 --> 07:16.901
If you can't even draw these,
you'll never be a real knight.

07:16.902 --> 07:18.403
Stand up perfectly straight

07:18.404 --> 07:20.530
and softly pull your arms back.

07:20.531 --> 07:21.615
Hey, Fraternity.

07:22.199 --> 07:25.660
You see, I'm going to be
one of the castle knights here.

07:25.661 --> 07:26.703
Me too.

07:26.704 --> 07:29.582
I'm sure you will, if you learn from me.

07:30.249 --> 07:31.666
<i>That's right.</i>

07:31.667 --> 07:33.376
<i>I'm a knight of this castle,</i>

07:33.377 --> 07:36.297
<i>expected to be on the front lines
in times of emergency.</i>

07:37.590 --> 07:40.509
<i>I just wish I could be of help
at other times, too.</i>

07:41.427 --> 07:43.386
<i>Lord Bruno's a margrave, too.</i>

07:43.387 --> 07:46.723
<i>His territory might end up
being the first line of defense.</i>

07:46.724 --> 07:48.933
<i>I might never even see him again,</i>

07:48.934 --> 07:51.186
<i>and yesterday will just be a fond memory.</i>

07:51.187 --> 07:52.688
Chilly!

07:53.480 --> 07:55.565
You look as cold as ever.

07:55.566 --> 07:57.902
Perhaps I should give you
a fur coat as well?

08:02.990 --> 08:04.240
Oh, no, thank you!

08:04.241 --> 08:06.910
If a noble showers me
with too many nice gifts,

08:06.911 --> 08:09.495
my brothers will start to worry
about my chastity!

08:09.496 --> 08:11.290
I'll throw you in the dungeon.

08:13.334 --> 08:14.877
I need some help.

08:15.669 --> 08:16.962
Come up here, please.

08:18.214 --> 08:19.923
Wait, what is this?

08:19.924 --> 08:21.633
A nutria?

08:21.634 --> 08:25.638
I hear this castle's dungeons
are filthy as hell, Chilly.

08:26.722 --> 08:28.224
Meet my pet, Little Squirrel.

08:29.058 --> 08:32.310
We were out for a walk,
but it got exhausted and fell asleep.

08:32.311 --> 08:34.479
I wish to have it practice climbing trees.

08:34.480 --> 08:36.857
Could you help me carry it to the woods?

08:37.942 --> 08:39.359
Your brother was in here crying.

08:39.360 --> 08:41.737
Don't get overly familiar
with just anybody.

08:43.697 --> 08:45.782
Your Highness!

08:45.783 --> 08:48.243
- Shall we do some flower embroidery?
- Pardon me.

08:48.244 --> 08:51.830
I must leave here at once.
Wake up, you meatball!

08:53.332 --> 08:56.251
- Your Highness?
- Lord Bruno, if you're in a hurry,

08:56.252 --> 08:59.754
the forest is home to foxes,
so we should go to the upper garden.

08:59.755 --> 09:00.964
Your Highness!

09:00.965 --> 09:03.425
- Chilly?
- Where are you, Princess?

09:06.887 --> 09:10.848
Beast-Tamer could help,
but he's in the storeroom today.

09:10.849 --> 09:11.976
Like this?

09:12.476 --> 09:13.394
That's right.

09:25.572 --> 09:30.286
Why won't it wake up in a stranger's arms?
It's sorely lacking in survival instinct.

09:30.911 --> 09:34.373
Little Squirrel has a rather
easygoing personality.

09:35.040 --> 09:38.460
That said, what should we do now?

09:41.463 --> 09:44.049
Chilly, do you go on boats a lot?

09:44.717 --> 09:47.176
Sometimes, to fish for trout.

09:47.177 --> 09:51.472
Do one-day-old boats tend to sink a lot?

09:51.473 --> 09:52.390
What?

09:52.391 --> 09:56.729
I got on one for marriage talks recently,
and it sprang a leak.

09:57.521 --> 09:59.981
And this is nothing new.

09:59.982 --> 10:02.276
You... You're having marriage talks?

10:04.028 --> 10:05.737
Am I not allowed to?

10:05.738 --> 10:08.449
I'll have you know
every one of them has failed.

10:09.033 --> 10:11.909
There are no fires allowed
in the dungeons, even in winter.

10:11.910 --> 10:14.495
Failed? But why?

10:14.496 --> 10:15.622
And that's not all.

10:16.248 --> 10:17.623
I've seen fires, thunderstorms,

10:17.624 --> 10:20.835
dead fish at a fishery we visited,

10:20.836 --> 10:22.796
<i>and horses going berserk.</i>

10:23.422 --> 10:26.759
Nothing good ever comes of them.
I believe I must be cursed.

10:27.217 --> 10:28.551
<i>Maybe that just means</i>

10:28.552 --> 10:32.014
<i>somebody doesn't want
Lord Bruno's marriage talks succeeding?</i>

10:32.598 --> 10:35.475
<i>Like, say, there's a woman
who's in love with him.</i>

10:35.476 --> 10:39.187
<i>She might be meddling to ensure
that the talks don't go smoothly.</i>

10:39.188 --> 10:41.898
<i>If it happens every time,</i>

10:41.899 --> 10:44.400
<i>it must be someone close to him.</i>

10:44.401 --> 10:46.737
What? You look like
you have something to say.

10:49.990 --> 10:53.034
Even if somebody has put a curse on you,

10:53.035 --> 10:55.453
I'd be fine if the boat caught fire.

10:55.454 --> 10:57.663
So I thought we could take one
out together now,

10:57.664 --> 10:59.916
but you aren't having
marriage talks today.

10:59.917 --> 11:04.253
Two guys going boating
would only look like a fishing trip.

11:04.254 --> 11:06.589
I'm sorry I couldn't be of help.

11:06.590 --> 11:08.884
No, that's not a bad idea.

11:09.468 --> 11:10.928
It might be worth a shot.

11:13.430 --> 11:15.807
Try to look like you're enjoying yourself.

11:15.808 --> 11:18.394
If nothing comes of it,
it'll provide consolation.

11:34.076 --> 11:35.786
That's a big trout.

11:36.453 --> 11:38.663
Does this castle serve fish for dinner?

11:38.664 --> 11:40.665
I'll let the chef know you asked for it.

11:40.666 --> 11:43.127
Would you prefer it grilled or stewed?

11:43.961 --> 11:46.588
Will you be staying here
a while, Lord Bruno?

11:47.172 --> 11:48.340
Yes... Yes, I will.

11:48.924 --> 11:50.425
I visit pretty often.

11:50.426 --> 11:52.886
I see. That's great to hear.

11:55.681 --> 11:58.517
Try to make your joy
a little less obvious, Chilly.

11:59.852 --> 12:05.232
Right, I really have been thinking
how sad I'd be if I never saw you again.

12:26.253 --> 12:27.671
Hey!

12:28.964 --> 12:31.508
The wind's too strong.

12:32.509 --> 12:36.430
The trees in the courtyard are rustling.

12:38.599 --> 12:39.433
Is that so?

12:40.350 --> 12:42.518
Nothing to share here.

12:42.519 --> 12:44.270
You, Feverish?

12:44.271 --> 12:47.232
This wind actually feels pleasant to me.

12:48.567 --> 12:51.278
I see Chilly in the upper garden.

12:53.155 --> 12:55.781
This wind seems to be coming
from where he is.

12:55.782 --> 12:59.995
Did he get himself
mixed up in something weird?

13:08.837 --> 13:11.340
<i>The weather's so nice, and yet...</i>

13:13.967 --> 13:17.095
<i>Why is it suddenly as cold
as the turn of the year?</i>

13:17.804 --> 13:20.641
What's the matter, Chilly?
Are you all right?

13:21.767 --> 13:25.020
<i>It seems Lord Bruno is just fine.</i>

13:26.438 --> 13:29.483
<i>But I really can't handle the cold.</i>

13:30.234 --> 13:32.110
<i>Remind me what your purpose is.</i>

13:34.655 --> 13:35.489
<i>To heroically...</i>

13:37.115 --> 13:38.492
<i>rescue...</i>

13:39.243 --> 13:41.411
<i>a princess someday.</i>

13:42.829 --> 13:45.207
<i>But how am I supposed to do that...</i>

13:47.876 --> 13:49.836
<i>when I'm this helpless?</i>

13:52.130 --> 13:53.715
<i>I might never be able to.</i>

14:03.850 --> 14:05.018
So warm.

14:08.230 --> 14:09.982
I'm all right now.

14:10.983 --> 14:13.694
Your hair changed color, Chilly.

14:14.194 --> 14:16.989
Yes, my hair changes color
depending on how I'm feeling.

14:17.698 --> 14:18.949
Really?

14:20.409 --> 14:21.660
Really.

14:23.870 --> 14:24.871
I'm sorry.

14:25.831 --> 14:28.584
I'll state it plainly because
"consolation" isn't good enough.

14:29.418 --> 14:33.838
I'm certain that somebody is trying
to keep you away from others.

14:33.839 --> 14:38.010
It's likely that your marriage talks
were all sabotaged.

14:38.635 --> 14:43.390
But, as this is a willful act,
it can be resolved.

14:44.641 --> 14:45.726
It will be resolved.

14:55.319 --> 14:57.320
<i>I said all that,</i>

14:57.321 --> 15:01.325
<i>but if it does get resolved,
Lord Bruno will marry.</i>

15:02.409 --> 15:06.038
<i>Not that I'm hoping for anything.</i>

15:07.623 --> 15:11.668
<i>To think I'd find serving someone
beautiful... What am I, the castellan?</i>

15:12.336 --> 15:13.670
Hey, Chilly!

15:14.254 --> 15:16.797
What is that? A beaver kin?

15:16.798 --> 15:18.258
This is...

15:19.092 --> 15:21.218
My pet, Little Squirrel.

15:21.219 --> 15:24.096
What? Squirrel? You must be stupid.

15:24.097 --> 15:25.973
How could you fatten it up so much?

15:25.974 --> 15:27.933
This is the problem with rich noble kids.

15:27.934 --> 15:31.687
Chilly, that's the first time
anybody's ever called me stupid.

15:31.688 --> 15:34.899
That's just how Swordsman is.
He's not a bad guy, though.

15:34.900 --> 15:36.150
Listen up.

15:36.151 --> 15:39.528
When you feed it from now,
toss the food around and make it walk.

15:39.529 --> 15:42.616
Give it regular exercise so it won't
hurt its legs when it has to run.

15:43.492 --> 15:45.576
Let's weigh it for starters.

15:45.577 --> 15:48.163
We can use the scales in the storeroom.

15:50.707 --> 15:52.834
Follow me, and hurry!

15:54.294 --> 15:56.755
What are you looking at, Insomniac?

15:57.381 --> 16:00.550
Even you wouldn't survive
a fall from that height.

16:01.093 --> 16:04.220
No, it's just that I heard my brothers.

16:04.221 --> 16:05.722
Is that so?

16:07.224 --> 16:09.183
It's fun watching the kids.

16:09.184 --> 16:12.561
Managing the estate's books, not so much.

16:12.562 --> 16:14.940
Who should I ask to help me
while you're away?

16:15.524 --> 16:19.277
Your family has done this for generations,
but it's still a lot of work.

16:20.070 --> 16:21.821
As for your aides,

16:21.822 --> 16:26.243
it's going to be Eleonora and Johannes,
heir to the lord of a western territory.

16:26.868 --> 16:27.785
Ellie?

16:27.786 --> 16:29.454
And what of the marriage?

16:30.163 --> 16:32.081
I haven't told her yet,

16:32.082 --> 16:36.044
but I will make sure to before you leave
for the Country of Long Nights.

16:37.087 --> 16:39.714
The Country of Long Nights is a quiet,

16:39.715 --> 16:44.261
beautiful place where the moonlight
forms rainbows in the night sky.

16:45.470 --> 16:48.723
All these countries
that you brothers will be visiting...

16:48.724 --> 16:51.767
Should you find them
comfortable to live in,

16:51.768 --> 16:54.145
you're free to remain there if you wish.

16:54.146 --> 16:56.564
That's how Baribara feels.

16:56.565 --> 16:58.023
No, but I...

16:58.024 --> 17:01.778
You and your younger brothers
aren't weak anymore.

17:02.362 --> 17:04.406
You're strong enough
to live as you see fit.

17:14.750 --> 17:17.835
I'll be checking to see if it's gotten
any lighter next week, okay?

17:17.836 --> 17:19.004
No slacking off.

17:19.588 --> 17:21.213
<i>What are they doing?</i>

17:21.214 --> 17:24.468
<i>I don't really want to
get involved in their matters.</i>

17:31.933 --> 17:32.851
What's with you?

17:34.102 --> 17:37.188
I was gathering firewood,
and I think a thorn got me.

17:37.189 --> 17:39.106
Wait, seriously?

17:39.107 --> 17:41.108
You don't train enough.

17:41.109 --> 17:42.359
Justice.

17:42.360 --> 17:46.155
Hungry, I saw you slacking off
during training yesterday.

17:46.156 --> 17:48.116
I'll train you myself, starting now.

17:49.201 --> 17:50.660
Where do you think you're going?

17:51.286 --> 17:54.163
Ow! Cut it out!

17:54.164 --> 17:59.084
You dare ignore Master Justice,
nephew of the chancellor? How rude.

17:59.085 --> 18:02.087
Aren't you a knight? Then act like it.

18:02.088 --> 18:05.299
Unhand me! You're going to ruin
my beautiful long hair!

18:05.300 --> 18:07.551
Young Master, Hungry seems mighty pleased.

18:07.552 --> 18:09.553
I am highly displeased!

18:09.554 --> 18:11.013
What's going on here?

18:11.014 --> 18:12.516
Now, Hungry!

18:13.308 --> 18:14.476
Hey!

18:15.519 --> 18:18.438
If you've got something to say,
I'll hear you out.

18:20.857 --> 18:23.984
I'll disinfect your finger.
Let's go upstairs.

18:23.985 --> 18:25.111
Okay.

18:25.695 --> 18:29.366
Also, I think I'm going to be hungry soon.

18:29.866 --> 18:34.078
That's bad news!
You can't wait until dinner, can you?

18:34.079 --> 18:35.579
All right, come on.

18:35.580 --> 18:40.042
I'll make you some venison steak with
rose sauce and cranberries on the side.

18:40.043 --> 18:40.961
Hooray!

18:41.711 --> 18:46.258
Why does dealing with you brothers
have to be so damn exhausting?

18:53.431 --> 18:55.350
<i>As his day of departure grew closer,</i>

18:56.017 --> 18:58.979
<i>Insomniac was busy
making travel preparations.</i>

18:59.896 --> 19:04.650
Listen, Insomniac.
The Country of Long Nights is cold.

19:04.651 --> 19:05.943
I know that.

19:05.944 --> 19:08.780
I've been to that border before.

19:09.406 --> 19:12.783
I've never traveled
any farther than the town,

19:12.784 --> 19:16.245
but I know that place
is far colder than the border.

19:16.246 --> 19:20.583
I'll fish out the castellan's
old fur coat. Take it with you.

19:20.584 --> 19:23.461
Thanks. I appreciate your help, Lavinia.

19:24.045 --> 19:25.796
And then we'll take care of food.

19:25.797 --> 19:29.967
That freezing land can't have
anything better than bitterly cold tea.

19:29.968 --> 19:31.468
Surely it can't be that bad.

19:31.469 --> 19:35.848
Good grief. How long will His Majesty
let that female general have her way?

19:35.849 --> 19:40.687
We have plenty of pureblood
general lineages of our own.

19:41.271 --> 19:45.524
But think of Baribara's exploits
during the Great Panic.

19:45.525 --> 19:49.361
What's more, she is a legend
from the Country of Might.

19:49.362 --> 19:53.909
Putting her front and center acts
as a deterrent to our northern neighbors.

19:54.492 --> 19:55.784
I understand your point,

19:55.785 --> 19:57.536
but now I hear that she plans on

19:57.537 --> 20:00.915
marrying one of her monster sons
off to the castellan's only daughter.

20:00.916 --> 20:02.207
What?

20:02.208 --> 20:05.377
Then the post of castellan
will be under her thumb, too?

20:05.378 --> 20:06.795
<i>Good.</i>

20:06.796 --> 20:09.049
<i>This isn't about my brothers.</i>

20:09.799 --> 20:10.925
<i>It's just about me.</i>

20:10.926 --> 20:13.218
Those are lords from the west.

20:13.219 --> 20:15.680
Just wait. I'll go tell them what's what.

20:16.264 --> 20:17.556
It's fine.

20:17.557 --> 20:19.392
Can you hold this for a bit?

20:21.728 --> 20:23.605
I should go say hello.

20:24.189 --> 20:27.067
It's a pleasure, lords.

20:27.692 --> 20:30.153
Trust you to have
your fingers on the pulse.

20:31.279 --> 20:33.238
You must be Johannes's father.

20:33.239 --> 20:35.283
I look forward to working with him.

20:37.827 --> 20:39.745
Lady Baribara's oldest.

20:39.746 --> 20:42.290
Well done securing your spot
as the next castellan.

20:42.874 --> 20:44.793
That won't be for a while yet.

20:45.293 --> 20:46.835
But in a few decades' time,

20:46.836 --> 20:49.755
I'll be His Majesty's proxy
whenever he is away

20:49.756 --> 20:51.758
and managing the kingdom's territory.

20:52.550 --> 20:54.803
I hope to have your support
when the time comes.

20:56.137 --> 20:57.846
Speaking of the west,

20:57.847 --> 21:02.686
I hear black markets for excess produce
have cropped up these past few years.

21:03.561 --> 21:08.190
I look forward to seeing how your heirs
develop your economies going forward.

21:08.191 --> 21:10.401
Black markets? How scandalous!

21:10.402 --> 21:12.654
Where did you hear that?

21:15.031 --> 21:17.367
<i>It's all right. I can do this.</i>

21:18.660 --> 21:20.370
<i>I'm not a child anymore.</i>

21:20.870 --> 21:23.206
<i>Nothing like that will ever happen again.</i>

21:24.249 --> 21:25.792
<i>If I don't stay on top of things,</i>

21:26.376 --> 21:28.670
<i>who will look out for my little brothers?</i>

21:29.504 --> 21:30.755
Insomniac!

21:31.256 --> 21:32.756
Lavinia. I'll take those.

21:32.757 --> 21:34.383
That's not it.

21:34.384 --> 21:38.220
Are you really going to marry Eleonora?

21:38.221 --> 21:41.057
Is the castellan forcing you into it?

21:41.933 --> 21:46.062
I am. She gets along with my brothers,

21:46.813 --> 21:50.775
and she's the only woman I know
who Swordsman can really talk to.

21:51.818 --> 21:54.695
Ellie herself said she wasn't picky.

21:54.696 --> 21:57.490
As the oldest, I should see
that she's taken care of.

21:57.991 --> 22:02.495
You're going to join the castellan family
and its 1,500-year history for that?

22:03.079 --> 22:06.082
You'd better take responsibility
for your decisions.

22:07.375 --> 22:10.419
Okay, back to travel preparations.

22:10.420 --> 22:13.089
Yeah, yeah. Don't come crying to me later.

22:13.631 --> 22:14.965
<i>Mama and the castellan say</i>

22:14.966 --> 22:17.802
<i>that I'm free to remain
in the Country of Long Nights if I wish.</i>

22:19.888 --> 22:23.224
<i>But I'm going to marry Ellie</i>

22:23.933 --> 22:25.560
<i>and become the castellan one day.</i>

22:26.561 --> 22:28.855
<i>Then there will be no need to worry.</i>

22:30.190 --> 22:31.858
<i>I'll be all right now.</i>

22:34.360 --> 22:36.446
<i>What's all the fuss about?</i>

22:37.030 --> 22:40.200
My, you're here too, Sir Insomniac?

22:40.909 --> 22:42.452
Hello there, Miss Anna-Marie.

22:45.330 --> 22:48.708
<i>Princess Brunhild
is a mere 1.5 meters away.</i>

22:49.292 --> 22:51.920
<i>That's a new record.
I should note it down later.</i>

22:52.879 --> 22:56.758
It's the monthly tournament.
We're in the semifinals.

22:58.093 --> 22:59.135
Right, that was today.

23:00.136 --> 23:02.971
Maybe I should've entered, too.
It has been a while.

23:02.972 --> 23:04.474
Look.

23:07.769 --> 23:09.896
It's the most hotly anticipated matchup,

23:10.688 --> 23:13.441
Eleonora versus Swordsman.

24:47.285 --> 24:50.246
I think I might be able to beat you soon.

24:51.331 --> 24:54.334
<i>I feel like I'm drifting
farther and farther away</i>

24:54.918 --> 24:58.503
<i>from those days
when my heart was never troubled.</i>

24:58.504 --> 25:00.965
RECKLESSNESS
